!! Proposed Definitions And Examples

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: be'e (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to make a request to speak.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* Request to send

!!!See Also
* ju'i
* ta'a

!!!Usage Examples
;be'e nolni'u io : ''Pardon me, ma'am.''
;re'i : ''Yes?''
;.e'o ga'i nai ko dunda lo sicni : ''Can you spare a dime?''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: co'o (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to express an acknowledgement of parting.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* bye-bye
* goodbye
* farewell
* so long
* adieu
* Godspeed

!!!See Also
* tolrinsa

!!!Usage Examples
;co'o ro do : ''Goodbye, everyone!''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: coi (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to express greeting.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* hi
* hello
* howdy
* hail
* salaam

!!!See Also
* rinsa

!!!Usage Examples
;coi pe mi pendo do mo : ''Hello my friend, what are you up to?''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: fe'o (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to indicate the end of a conversation or discussion.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* over and out

!!!Usage Examples
;.ai mi na stali lo nu tirna ti .i fe'o : ''I'm not staying to listen to this! Have a nice day!''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: fi'i (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to greet cordially a visitor or recent arrival, express hospitality.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* welcome
* make yourself at home

!!!Usage Examples
;fi'i .djan. mi'a denpa tu'a do : ''Welcome, John! We were waiting for you.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: fi'i nai (COI*)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to express inhospitality.

!!!Usage Examples
;le'o ko na rivbi fi'i nai palci je tolvri danlu : ''Grr! Avoid not, unwelcome evil and cowardly beast!''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: je'e (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to indicate reception of a message, acknowledge offers and thanks.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* roger
* got it
* gotcha
* okay
* you're welcome

!!!Usage Examples
;zo .faidon. cu pagbu cy. ly. ly. : ''"faidon" is in CLL.''
;je'e : ''Okay.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: je'e nai (COI*)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to deny acknowledgement or indicate that a message was not understood.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* excuse me?
* pardon?

!!!Usage Examples
;je'e nai .i mi na jimpe : ''Sorry, I don't understand.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: ju'i (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to attract attention.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* hey

!!!Usage Examples
;ju'i lobypli : ''Hey, Lojbanist!''
;ju'i .djan. ko catlu ti : ''Hey, John, look at this.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: ju'i cu'i (COI*)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to suggest a normal level of attention, for instance as a command for troops to assume a relaxed position.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* at ease

!!!Usage Examples
;ju'i cu'i sonci : ''At ease, soldiers.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: ju'i nai (COI*)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to draw attention away from oneself.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* ignore me
* nevermind

!!!Usage Examples
;ua mi ba'o tolcri ju'i nai : ''Oh, I found it, nevermind.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: ke'o (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to ask for repetition.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* please repeat

!!!See Also
* je'e nai

!!!Usage Examples
;ke'o do'u mi na pu tirna : ''What did you say? I didn't hear.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: ke'o nai (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to express that an utterance does not need to be repeated.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* you don't need to repeat

!!!See Also
* je'e

!!!Usage Examples
;ke'o nai do mi'a pu tirna ca lo krefu be fi li pa : ''All right, we heard you the first time.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: ki'e (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to express gratitude.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* thanks

!!!Usage Examples
;ki'e sai .i ti melbi : ''Thank you very much! It's beautiful.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: ki'e nai (COI*)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to express that an expected help was not received.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* no thanks to you

!!!Usage Examples
;mi ba'o facki ki'e nai : ''I've found it myself, no thanks to you!''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: mi'e (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Used for self-introduction.

!!!Usage Examples
;coi mi'e nolraitru be le munje : ''Hi, I'm the King of the Universe.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: mi'e nai (COI*)
!!!Proposed Definition
Use for denial of identity.

!!!Usage Examples
;coi djan : ''Hi, John.''
;mi'e nai djan : ''I'm not John.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: mu'o (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to give up the floor.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* over

!!!Usage Examples
;do ma zvati mu'o : ''What's your location? Over.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: mu'o nai (COI*)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to continue to hold the floor.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* more to come

!!!Usage Examples
;i je ko'a ma mi cusku pau nai mu'o nai : ''And what did they tell me?''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: nu'e (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to make a promise.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* I promise.

!!!Usage Examples
;nu'e do'u mi ba xruti za lo cacra be li me'i pa : ''I promise I'll be back in less than an hour.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: nu'e cu'i (COI*)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to indicate that one is not promising anything.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* no promises

!!!Usage Examples
;.a'i sai mi cpacu va'u do nu'e cu'i : ''I'll do my best to get it for you, but I don't promise anything.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: nu'e nai (COI*)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to take back a promise.

!!!Usage Examples
;nu'e do'u mi na za'u re'u pante ca le cabdei .i .yy go'i nu'e nai .i .oi ti rigni : ''I promise I won't complain again today. Umm... I better take that back. This stinks!''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: pe'u (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to make a polite request.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* please

!!!Usage Examples
;pe'u do'u ko na dunda lo cidja le danlu : ''Please don't feed the animals.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: re'i (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to express readiness to listen.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* ready to receive

!!!Usage Examples
;re'i do'u do ma sisku : ''Yes? What were you looking for?''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: re'i nai (COI*)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to indicate not being ready to listen or pay attention.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* not ready to receive

!!!Usage Examples
;ko denpa ze'a lo mentu re'i nai : ''Just wait a minute please.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: ta'a (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to interrupt.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* excuse me
* pardon me

!!!Usage Examples
;ta'a da ma stuzi lo vimku'a : ''Excuse me, could someone tell me where the bathroom is?''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: vi'o (COI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to indicate readiness to comply.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* wilco (ack and will comply)
* will do

!!!Usage Examples
;pe'u do'u ko kargau lo canko : ''Could you please open a window?''
;vi'o : ''Sure.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: doi (DOI)
!!!Proposed Definition
Vocative. Used to identify intended listener.

!!!Usage Examples
;ko ti klama doi gerku : ''Come here doggie.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: do'u (DOhU)
!!!Proposed Definition
Terminator for COI and DOI phrases.
!!!Proposed Keywords
* end vocative

!!!See Also
* doi
* be'e
* co'o
* coi
* fe'o
* fi'i
* je'e
* ju'i
* ke'o
* ki'e
* mi'e
* mu'o
* nu'e
* pe'u
* re'i
* ta'a
* vi'o
{BOX}

!! Notes

* __coi co'o__ and __doi do'u__  were removed. No special definition needed.

*__nu'e cu'i__ was changed to "non-promise", becasue "promise realease" didn't seem to fit the scale. To release someone else from a promise one could use perhaps __nu'e nai dai__?

* Merge ''COI'' and ''DOI'' post-dotside? — donri
